Also, I think set_cppo(mode = "fast") should set -march=native

http://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc/i386-and-x86_002d64-Options.html

It is a gcc-ism, so CRAN wouldn't let us set it; although we might want to do so for command-line Stan (at the cost of slightly more weird differences in the binaries). It seems that clang++ honors it, but I don't know about all compilers.

But I managed to knock almost 2 minutes off of test-models with it set:
goodrich@CYBERPOWERPC:/opt/stan$ make clean-all && time make CC=g++-4.7 O=3 -j8 test-models > /tmp/g++4.7plain.log && echo "success"
...
real    22m59.062s
user    138m13.714s
sys     4m12.156s
success

goodrich@CYBERPOWERPC:/opt/stan$ nano makefile
goodrich@CYBERPOWERPC:/opt/stan$ make clean-all && time make CC=g++-4.7 O=3 -j8 test-models > /tmp/g++4.7native.log && echo "success"
...
real    21m8.914s
user    139m11.065s
sys     4m23.052s
success
goodrich@CYBERPOWERPC:/opt/stan$

Ben

