With overloading, there's usually the issue of
which variables to drop first if they're not
named.

The same issue comes up if we want to support
this kind of thing:

   -- normal          (y|mu,sigma)
   -- centered normal (y|sigma)
   -- unit normal     (y)

Then, there's versions with precision params:

   -- normal precision (y|mu,tau)
   -- centered normal precision (y|tau)

Without named arguments, I'd go for verbose names.
It's easier to read code that way, but harder to
write (you have to look up the names of things).

