On Monday, October 15, 2012 9:56:51 PM UTC-4, Matt Hoffman wrote:
> This bug (which I just pushed a fix for) sometimes results in bad
> behavior.

This patch adds a couple of asserts(), and we already had a few others:

goodrich@CYBERPOWERPC:/opt/stan$ git grep -n "assert(" src/ | cat
src/stan/mcmc/adaptive_cdhmc.hpp:153:        assert(x.size() == _x.size());
src/stan/mcmc/adaptive_cdhmc.hpp:154:        assert(z.size() == _z.size());
src/stan/mcmc/hmc_base.hpp:142:          assert(params_r->size() == model.num_params_r());
src/stan/mcmc/hmc_base.hpp:146:          assert(params_i->size() == model.num_params_i());
src/stan/mcmc/hmc_base.hpp:168:        assert(x.size() == this->_x.size());
src/stan/mcmc/hmc_base.hpp:169:        assert(z.size() == this->_z.size());
src/stan/meta/traits.hpp:150:    // assert((length(x1) == 1) || (length(x1) == result));
src/stan/meta/traits.hpp:151:    // assert((length(x2) == 1) || (length(x2) == result));
src/stan/meta/traits.hpp:160:    // assert((length(x1) == 1) || (length(x1) == result));
src/stan/meta/traits.hpp:161:    // assert((length(x2) == 1) || (length(x2) == result));
src/stan/meta/traits.hpp:162:    // assert((length(x3) == 1) || (length(x3) == result));
src/test/io/reader_test.cpp:680:  assert(solver.eigenvalues()[0] > 1E-10);
src/test/io/reader_test.cpp:706:  assert(solver.eigenvalues()[0] > 1E-10);
src/test/io/reader_test.cpp:769:  assert(solver.eigenvalues()[0] > 1E-10); // check positive definite with smallest eigenvalue > 0
src/test/io/reader_test.cpp:795:  assert(solver.eigenvalues()[0] > 1E-10); // check positive definite with smallest eigenvalue > 0

I am not sure what to throw in this case (Daniel?), but if an assert() is triggered it would take down the process if it were called from R. I think asserts get disabled if NDEBUG is defined, but we should probably replace these with something else to be on the safe side.

Ben

From u8aa9b8cc06fdc99c at groups.google.com  Tue Oct 16 21:39:39 2012
From: u8aa9b8cc06fdc99c at groups.google.com (Bob Carpenter)
