Once we get the code in place to give model file line numbers with exceptions, we will also be able to easily check for lp__ == -inf and issue meaningful error messages without needing the *_log functions to throw exceptions.  We will still need to make that check due to potential underflow or programming issues with people directly manipulating lp__.

The other possibility is to make the behaviour configurable, eg, with a template parameter.  Calls that happen as the result of a ~ statement could throw exceptions and all other calls return -inf for out of bounds behaviour.

Cheers,
Marcus

