A couple of comments on Ben's answer there.

1. run a model in parallel in Stan, say, dogs is a compiled model:
./dogs --seed=12345 --chain_id=1
./dogs --seed=12345 --chain_id=2

The point is that you have to specify the same seed for the results you desired.  Personally, I do not care about correlation at that level.

2. clang might not work well on old Mac say even Snow Leopard for rstan (ie, old version in Xcode), I will report some details later.

