On 10/21/12 9:57 AM, Jiqiang Guo wrote:

> 1. run a model in parallel in Stan, say, dogs is a compiled model:
> ./dogs --seed=12345 --chain_id=1
> ./dogs --seed=12345 --chain_id=2
>
> The point is that you have to specify the same seed for the results you desired.  Personally, I do not care about
> correlation at that level.

If you do this in Stan from the command line and
don't generate your own seed, the time-based
seeding is likely to give both processes exactly
the same random seed.  And that we definitely don't
want.

This shouldn't be such an issue with R if you generate
random seeds for the chains from the same R session.

> 2. clang might not work well on old Mac say even Snow Leopard for rstan (ie, old version in Xcode), I will report some
> details later.

That's where we developed most of Stan.  Is there
something particular you're worried about?

- Bob

