MacPorts is an alternative, but it only goes
current + two previous OSes
(now Mountain Lion, Lion, Snow Leopard).

We could suggest MacPorts on the Wiki, but it looks
to be a pretty complicated install and I can't
replicate it for Snow Leopard.

Also, the MacPorts stuff says it depends on having
at least some version of Xcode installed, so I'm not
even sure this would work if you can't get Xcode
any more.

I just kept updating my own machines to make sure
we ran with the latest.  And I can't even keep the
stupid names straight -- I'm actually on Mountain Lion.

>     As far as integration with R, no idea.  I think g++
>     is built in.
>
>
> The binary doesn't include any compilers. Some compiler collection is necessary to build R from source, but not
> specifically gcc I don't think.

Ah, right.  I think what's going on is that
the makefile comes with g++ -O2 specified.

- Bob

