> > > I propose that the default seed for Stan be -1 (which would indicate to generate a seed from the clock time and
> > > chain_id) and the default seed for stan() should also be -1. However, I was surprised to find that specifying --seed=-1
> > > works currently
> >
> > I think the default behavior should be to choose
> > a random seed, not use -1.
> >
> > Seeds are unsigned int in Stan (because they're
> > uint32_t in Boost).
>
> If stan() is going to be passing a seed, then stan() is limited to signed integers because R doesn't have an unsigned integer type. So, there might be sequences that someone could do in Stan that wouldn't be possible to replicate with rstan. Maybe reserve 0 as the code for "generate a seed from the time and chain_id"?

