That is fine, although ideally the two PDFs should be the same except for the coloring and 1 page at the end of the diffed PDF that links to the pages with changes.

> Will alltt handle ~ inline properly (that is, not
> make it a superscript and put it in the right font)?

I'll have to look into that. What are you doing now to make the tildes look right? When I compile this on my laptop, the tildes are too small and too high:

\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{times}
%\usepackage{alltt}
\usepackage{fancyvrb}
\begin{document}

\begin{Verbatim}
data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  int<lower=0,upper=1> y[N];
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0,upper=1> theta;
}
model {
  theta ~ beta(1,1);
  for (n in 1:N)
    y[n] ~ bernoulli(theta);
}
\end{Verbatim}

\end{document}

Ben

