Why do you say that?  In Stan, we get:

beta_log(1e-100,0.8,0.8) = 45.635
beta_log(1e-300,0.8,0.8) = 137.738
beta_log(1e-323,0.8,0.8) = 148.333

It's the same to 6 decimal places, at least!

It's the gradient that's problematic, not the value.

