Something must be going on with the combination of the transformation and the gradient. Even for very small theta, the derivative with respect to theta should be decently behaved. Like

> theta <- 1e-300
> -0.2 * (1 / theta - 1 / (1 - theta))
[1] -2e+299

The 1 - x piece underflows to 1.0 but that is okay. I guess that when you multiply that by the derivative of theta wrt the unbounded parameter, there could be problems. But even that looks like it should work

> unbounded <- -700
> theta <- plogis(unbounded)
> -0.2 * (1 / theta - 1 / (1 - theta)) * dlogis(unbounded)
[1] -0.2

Ben

