>
>     On Monday, October 29, 2012 4:34:48 PM UTC-4, Marcus Brubaker wrote:
>
>         On a side note, is it possible to fork() and trap the segfault when it's run in R?
>
>
>     Not under Windows because fork() isn't supported.
>
>         Or run the model in a separate process with an exec() call?
>
>
>     Maybe. I'll have to look into that.
>
>
> In theory it should be possible unless R has some restriction on calling exec().  The only problem is that it makes
> communicating back to R a little more complicated and it take some work to make it cross platform.

Once we went that far, it'd probably make sense
just to call the regular command line version and
pass the arguments to it, then collect the results
back in R.

Also, R wouldn't have to load the model to run into
R's own memory, so it could be configured to use any
compiler with any options we wanted.

- Bob

